WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.974
Welcome to Grade 7 English, Unit
1: Family, Identity, and History.

2
00:00:05.054 --> 00:00:08.497
This is Unit 1: Family, Identity, and History.

3
00:00:08.577 --> 00:00:16.691
In this unit, you will explore some of the most important
questions a person can ask: Where do I come from?

4
00:00:16.771 --> 00:00:19.141
Who are the people in my family?

5
00:00:19.221 --> 00:00:23.659
What stories have been passed down through the generations?

6
00:00:23.739 --> 00:00:29.173
You will read about families, learn
how to describe your own background,

7
00:00:29.253 --> 00:00:35.529
and discover how people across East Africa
and the wider world have moved, settled,

8
00:00:35.609 --> 00:00:38.515
and built new lives over the centuries.

9
00:00:38.595 --> 00:00:44.948
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

10
00:00:45.028 --> 00:00:53.579
By the end of this unit, you will be able to read and
understand a passage about family history and migration,

11
00:00:53.659 --> 00:00:56.168
and discuss its ideas in English.

12
00:00:56.248 --> 00:01:03.309
You will also use the past simple tense correctly
to describe completed actions and events.

13
00:01:03.389 --> 00:01:09.586
You will also distinguish between the
past simple and the present perfect tense.

14
00:01:09.666 --> 00:01:12.489
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

15
00:01:12.569 --> 00:01:19.808
Your vocabulary work begins with these words: belligerent,
malevolence, vindictive, infuriate, animosity, narcissistic.

16
00:01:19.888 --> 00:01:24.790
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

17
00:01:24.870 --> 00:01:28.664
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

18
00:01:28.744 --> 00:01:36.119
The reading sequence includes Keeping the Story Alive:
Oral History and Heritage and The Journey of Alina's Family.

19
00:01:36.199 --> 00:01:37.027
Read actively.

20
00:01:37.107 --> 00:01:41.500
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

21
00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:45.714
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

22
00:01:45.794 --> 00:01:49.391
The first language focus is The Past Simple Tense.

23
00:01:49.471 --> 00:01:55.937
The past simple tense describes actions and
events that started and finished in the past,

24
00:01:56.017 --> 00:01:58.806
which makes it the storyteller's tense.

25
00:01:58.886 --> 00:02:04.984
Almost every sentence in a biography, a
family history or a chronicle depends on it,

26
00:02:05.064 --> 00:02:08.735
so this unit treats it as your most important tool.

27
00:02:08.815 --> 00:02:16.752
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

28
00:02:16.832 --> 00:02:21.722
In speaking, you will complete Speaking
1: Present Your Family Biography.

29
00:02:21.802 --> 00:02:26.284
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

30
00:02:26.364 --> 00:02:29.756
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

31
00:02:29.836 --> 00:02:33.364
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

32
00:02:33.444 --> 00:02:35.082
You are ready to begin.

33
00:02:35.162 --> 00:02:42.475
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

34
00:02:42.555 --> 00:02:46.059
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

35
00:02:46.139 --> 00:02:54.348
Use AI English for hints and feedback any time, and bring
your questions to a live session too if you join one.
